  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU needs the optional RS485 interface. Functions 03, 05, 06 and 16; writes with address 0 are broadcast; reads in broadcast are ignored.",
    "8 data bits, 1 stop bit, none, even or odd parity and 1200 to 115200 bit/s, set with Addr, bAud and PrtY. The manual gives no factory address, baud rate or parity: check the screens on the indicator; no parity is assumed here.",
    "Every register is a signed 16-bit value. Most registers up to address 12 are read only.",
    "The process value, limits and alarm values are integers in the display unit, with the decimal places set in register 52 (dPPo); a temperature is read multiplied by 10 whatever that setting is.",
    "A write outside the allowed range is not refused: the indicator stores the maximum allowed value and returns it.",
    "The manual lists settings for four alarms (registers 18 to 29 and 38 to 41), but the indicator has two alarm outputs, as the status words and coils show.",
    "The manual prints 32400 for baud rate value 5, while the list of speeds has 38400; 38400 is used here.",
    "Registers 3, 14 to 16, 30 to 37, 45 to 49, 55, 59 to 66, 70 to 79 and 83 are reserved or for internal use.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
